| Fix the html; also convert math to LaTeX for Word
| This runs after the built-in html step and the formatting script
| 1;1 2015-3-19 cln
| 1;2 2015-6-25 cln: improving support for [e], [us], [ue], [os], and [oe].
|     also adding support for the TextWithinMath style.
| 1;3 2015-6-28 cln: changing style name TextWithinMath to math-TextInMath.
| 1;4 2015-06-29 cln: fixing support for math-TextInMath style.
|     Also adding various function names (although cannot be absolutely sure if these are meant as function names).
| 1;5 2017-07-29 improvements for math not enclosed by [ts] and [te] or math style
| 1;6 2019-03-27 improvements for the OneWordBridge style
| 1;7 2019-12-18 support for the new math-separation style
|     Also changing support for the math-TextInMath style.
| 1;9 - supporting [kps] and [kpe] codes with gather* structure.
| 1;10 - cln  preventing the insertion of $ $ for start math style followed immediately by start math-separation style.
| 1;11 - dfh fix glitch in ext2htm <it> should be underbar
| 1;12 2024-04-02/cln - some fixes for the OneWordBridge style
| states: 1 = normal text
|   6 = inside of math notation
|   7 = temporary math notation 
|   8 = temporary math notation, one level up 
|   9 = temporary math notation, two levels up 
|   11 = after \mathop{ before termination
|   12 = after \mathop{ before termination in temporary math notation
|   13 = after \mathop{ before termination in temporary math notation, one level up
|   14 = after \text{ before termination 
| 18 = between kps and kpe codes in technical notation
| 19 = after start math-separation, before end math-separation 
| Exception for math Codes in the math-separation style
